          "location": "plantation-gate"
        },
        {
          "turn": 1,
          "round": 2,
          "text": "While she fetched the water Farquhar asked the rider for news from the front, and the rider said the Yankees were repairing the railroads and preparing another advance, had put the Owl Creek bridge in order and built a stockade on the north bank, and that a posted order said any civilian caught interfering with the railroad would be summarily hanged; the bridge was about thirty miles off with only a picket post half a mile out and a single sentinel at the near end.",
