            {
              "character": "scout",
              "mode": "witnessed"
            }
          ],
          "location": "plantation-gate"
        },
        {
          "turn": 1,
          "round": 3,
          "text": "Farquhar asked, smiling, what a civilian could accomplish who eluded the picket and got the better of the sentinel; the rider recalled that a month ago the flood of last winter had lodged a great quantity of driftwood against the wooden pier at the near end of the bridge, now dry and likely to burn like tow.",
          "importance": 5,
