        {
          "turn": 3,
          "round": 1,
          "text": "Farquhar stood on the bridge with his wrists bound behind him and a rope around his neck, watched by the captain, the sergeant and two privates, a sentinel at each end of the bridge and a company of infantry at parade rest on the north slope; no one moved or spoke.",
